    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261">

                <pb facs="0385" n="300" xml:id="pg300"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72113/1141: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-11T20:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">November 11,
                                1919, 8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            November 13, 7.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department’s November 8, 6 p.m.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d261-f1"/> The addressdo
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">acuerdo</hi>] has not been published nor have I
                    been furnished promised written statement.</p>
                <p>Please refer to my despatch number 875<anchor n="28" xml:id="d261-f2"/> and
                    recent telegrams on this subject. Under special orders from the Alien Property
                    Custodian coffee is being removed from enemy properties as rapidly as possible.
                    Continued delay in effecting sales steadily advances the date on which any of
                    these properties can be transferred, which in turn means that plantations very
                    probably will be stripped before new owners take possession.</p>
                <p>Continued delay likewise affords encouragement of German owners of these
                    properties (who are arriving from abroad by every boat) and ample opportunity to
                    prepare plans whereby, with the very willing connivance of natives, they may
                    purchase these properties at prices <hi rendition="#italic">bona fide</hi>
                    business men would not pay.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
